# Auth tokens for the Sandcastle loop — copy to .sandcastle/.env.secrets and fill in.
# OPTIONAL: main.ts resolves each token env-first (process.env THEN this file), so if
# you export the two tokens in your shell profile (~/.bashrc) this file is not needed.
#
#   cp .sandcastle/.env.secrets.example .sandcastle/.env.secrets   # only if you don't export them
#
# Precedence: a token set in the environment WINS over a value here. If both are set
# with different values, main.ts uses the env value and warns. This file is the
# fallback for machines where you'd rather not export the tokens in the shell.
#
# ⚠ Auth tokens live HERE (or in the environment) — NEVER in .env.
# Sandcastle's resolveEnv merges ALL of .env into every sandbox, and a sandbox env
# can only add keys, never remove them. Two tokens in .env would both leak into
# every sandbox → claude-code sends the wrong token to the wrong base URL → 401.
# .env.secrets is gitignored and read only by main.ts, which bakes one token per
# sandbox based on the active profile. main.ts also throws at startup if .env
# declares any active provider's tokenKey, blocking that leak before any agent runs.
#
# Only the tokens the ACTIVE PROFILE's providers need are required. The defaults
# (config.ts) are the Split profile: zai (GLM/z.ai) implementer/planner + anthropic
# (Opus) reviewer, so both tokens below are needed. An Opus-only profile
# (SANDCASTLE_PROFILE=opus) needs only the Anthropic one. main.ts resolves them
# env-first and validates the required tokens at startup, not at the first sandbox.

# Provider "zai" — GLM via z.ai (Anthropic-compatible endpoint).
# Used by the planner + implementer in the Split profile.
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Provider "anthropic" — Anthropic direct (api.anthropic.com).
# Used by the reviewer in the Split profile, and by every role in the Opus profile.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
